ica 66.5 million years ago, fossil tracks show]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134194811.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/66-5-million-years-ago-a-t-rex-crossed-north-america-fossil-footprints-now-show-the-giant-dinosaur-walked-not-ran/articleshow/134194811.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/66-5-million-years-ago-a-t-rex-crossed-north-america-fossil-footprints-now-show-the-giant-dinosaur-walked-not-ran/articleshow/134194811.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134195066,imgsize-192685.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Feather found in dinosaur poop may explain how birds survived the asteroid that killed dinosaurs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134192826.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The 66-million-year-old feather found inside fossilised dinosaur poop may offer clues about why some birds survived the asteroid impact that killed most dinosaurs. Researchers found feathers, fish scales and bird bones in the coprolite. The feather’s primitive structure suggests insulation and moulting may have played a role in determining which birds survived.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-66-million-year-old-feather-was-found-inside-dinosaur-poop-it-may-explain-how-birds-survived-the-asteroid-that-killed-the-dinosaurs/articleshow/134192826.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/a-66-million-year-old-feather-was-found-inside-dinosaur-poop-it-may-explain-how-birds-survived-the-asteroid-that-killed-the-dinosaurs/articleshow/134192826.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134193898,imgsize-252730.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[9/11 grounded US flights, but strangers moved a liver 800 miles to save a baby]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134188087.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 2001, six-month-old Kareena needed a liver transplant and was too sick to leave hospital. When US flights were grounded after 9/11, strangers and Tennessee National Guard members moved the donor liver nearly 800 miles from Nashville to Houston. Twenty-five years later, Kareena has graduated from college and is studying health policy in law school.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2001-a-houston-baby-needed-a-liver-transplant-as-us-flights-were-grounded-strangers-moved-the-organ-800-miles-by-c-130-and-25-years-later-she-is-in-law-school/articleshow/134188087.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2001-a-houston-baby-needed-a-liver-transplant-as-us-flights-were-grounded-strangers-moved-the-organ-800-miles-by-c-130-and-25-years-later-she-is-in-law-school/articleshow/134188087.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T15:25:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134192686,imgsize-74630.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists used centuries-old aurora sightings: their method placed solar minima within 2 years with more than 90% reliability]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134179728.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ancient auroras are unlocking secrets of solar activity, offering scientists a glimpse into the Sun's behavior long before our time. By employing a new statistical method to analyze historical sky observations, researchers have pieced together eight distinct cycles of solar activity from 1560 to 1640. This intriguing study correlates well with various independent solar records, enhancing our understanding of solar dynamics pre-dating contemporary measurements.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/scientists-used-centuries-old-aurora-sightings-to-reconstruct-8-solar-cycles-from-1560-to-1640-their-method-placed-solar-minima-within-2-years-with-more-than-90-reliability/articleshow/134179728.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/scientists-used-centuries-old-aurora-sightings-to-reconstruct-8-solar-cycles-from-1560-to-1640-their-method-placed-solar-minima-within-2-years-with-more-than-90-reliability/articleshow/134179728.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T15:57:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134180164,imgsize-1475826.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin lab owner wanted in US over alleged $93 million Medicare fraud]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134193577.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Indian-origin lab owner wanted in US over alleged $93 million Medicare fraud]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-lab-owner-wanted-in-us-over-93m-medicare-fraud-suspect-may-be-in-hyderabad/articleshow/134193577.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-lab-owner-wanted-in-us-over-93m-medicare-fr